course: dictionary
lesson: 5994
title: In the meantime
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «In the meantime» is a phrase you use while you wait. The meantime is the time between two events. «The bus is late. In the meantime, I will read my book.» While you wait for the bus, you read.
explain: Meantime can also work alone as an adverb, meaning meanwhile or at the same time. «Dad is making tea; meantime, I set the table.» Two things happen together.
explain: Be careful: meantime is not the same word as mean. In Kyle's story, someone «suddenly turns mean», and mean there means unkind. The two words look alike, so check the sentence before you decide what they mean.
fact: The meantime is the time between two events.
fact: «In the meantime» means while you wait for something else to happen.
fact: «For the meantime» means for now.
fact: As an adverb, «meantime» means meanwhile, or at the same time.
fact: «Mean» on its own can mean unkind, but it is a different word from meantime.
exercise: «The bus is late. In the meantime, I will read my book.» What does in the meantime mean here? | Never, not at all | Before the bus is late | For the whole year | *While I wait for the bus
exercise: «Dad is making tea; meantime, I set the table.» Which word means at the same time? | making | table | *meantime | Dad
exercise: Ella says meantime and mean are the same word. Is she right? | Yes, they mean exactly the same | Yes, both mean very happy | No, meantime is a kind of food | *No, meantime means the time while you wait, and mean can mean unkind
test: «We wait for the rain to stop. For the meantime, we stay inside.» What does for the meantime mean? | For a long walk | For ever | Very loudly | *For now
test: Which phrase means while you wait for something else to happen? | Gone to the shop | *In the meantime | Every now and then | Once upon a time
exam: «The train is delayed; in the meantime, Priya reads.» What does in the meantime tell us about Priya? | She is unkind to the train | She never reads on trains | She reads before the train was ever planned | *She reads while she waits for the train
